Track 1: Slackwater Chews the Cable
- Story & Context: During a low-tide dredge beneath Hull's Victoria Pier, commercial diver Arlo Finch pried loose an unmarked 1977 steel cylinder, coughing against the stench of black sulfuric mud and battery acid as the sea-rotted cassette within cracked into daylight. Refusing to hand the artifact over to port authorities, Finch carried it straight to an illicit dry-dock party, patching the raw tape's terrifying, pitch-climbing warning risers straight into the main sound system. The sound system redlined as decades of maritime rust vibrated out of the warehouse rafters, and the room lost its mind to an infectious 126 BPM kick locked underneath a chilling sampled distress voice: "Tide turns slow, pull the cable down below."
